Assemble the workpaper only from source-current scope, classified breaks and task completion evidence. Keep verified facts separate from management explanations; attach each explanation to its source and leave any unproved explanation in residuals. Recalculate the presented residual only from the exact source line amounts already supplied; when no exact calculation artifact is supplied, do not claim a reconciled total. State the assertion's evidence boundary and block a clean conclusion while a material residual or open task remains.